<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!--
        Shared look for dialog windows (ConnectionEditorWindow and friends,
        including the TestHarness prototype windows built via the
        ui-feature-prototyp skill) - so a fix like "leave room for the
        scrollbar" only has to be made once here instead of being
        copy-pasted (and drifting) across every dialog that has an
        internally-scrolling list next to a right-aligned button/icon.

        Included from each Window's own Application.Styles (see App.axaml /
        TestHarnessApp.axaml) rather than declared once globally, and opted
        into per-control via Classes="..." rather than an implicit selector
        on the bare control type - a plain `ScrollViewer` selector would also
        reach into every ListBox's internal template (MainWindow's
        Events/Hints/Items lists), which don't have this problem and
        shouldn't silently change layout just because a dialog needed a fix.

        New dialog needs the same fix? Add the matching Classes="..." to its
        control - don't re-derive or copy-paste the Setter values.
    -->

    <!-- A ScrollViewer wrapping a list of rows that end in a right-aligned
         button/icon (checkbox + text + lock icon, or name + action buttons):
         the scrollbar itself eats space on the right, and without this
         padding it overlaps that right-aligned control once the list
         actually needs to scroll. See ConnectionEditorWindow.axaml's
         player-picker list for the original bug this fixed. 20px (not the
         original 10px) so the gap reads clearly even at a glance, not just
         under close inspection - the dialogs using this class widen their
         own default Width to compensate, so this doesn't eat into the
         content column. -->
    <Style Selector="ScrollViewer.dialog-list">
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0,0,20,0"/>
    </Style>
</Styles>
